OL,3,GNEWSAWoman hit by e-bike 'will be
OL,4,Amissed forever'
OL,5,
OL,6,FRelatives has paid tribute to a
OL,7,F"kind-hearted" woman struck and killed
OL,8,Fby an e-bike while crossing a road.
OL,10,FJoanne Doyle was stepping on to the
OL,11,Fpavement from a zebra crossing on Mount
OL,12,FVernon Street in Liverpool when she was
OL,13,Fhit by an electric-assisted bicycle at
OL,14,Fabout 15:35 BST on 7 July, Merseyside
OL,15,FPolice said.
OL,17,FHer family said the 57-year-old was "a
OL,18,Fkind-hearted, generous soul who always
OL,19,Fput others before herself".
